  "summary": "Preprints propagate or decompose genetic evidence over networks, lifting target-indication coverage from 5.1% to 9.5% and making Open Targets re-ranking auditable.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is converting genetic signal into target- or phenotype-level claims through network propagation and evidence decomposition. BRIDGE propagates genetic evidence over coupled protein and disease networks, raising target-indication coverage from 5.1% to 9.5%. An Open Targets re-ranking separates genetic from protein evidence channels for Alzheimer and Parkinson disease, improving curated-gene recall. A path-energy framework conditions inference over AlzKB and Hetionet on genomic model uncertainty to yield phenotype hypotheses. Upstream, variant interpretation relies on models: Evo2 is strongest among six genomic foundation models on LGMD-gene ClinVar variants with 501 bp context, and SpliceVarMech targets non-canonical splicing variants. BioSensor-X and the SHAP-FOL-ILP proteomics workflow are adjacent evidence-integration efforts. The new element is explicit, auditable, uncertainty-aware evidence handling.",
